
Armor mitigation in World of Warcraft is a defensive stat that lowers the amount of physical damage you take from enemy attacks. 

Fandom
How Armor Works
Reduction, Not Avoidance: Unlike dodging or parrying (which completely avoid an attack so you take zero damage), armor reduces the severity of a hit that actually connects. You still take damage, but it is smaller. 
The Cap: Armor damage reduction has a maximum cap, usually 75% against enemies of equal or greater level. 
Enemy Level Scaling: The effectiveness of your armor depends on your target's or attacker's level. Higher-level bosses require more armor to reach the same percentage of damage reduction. 
Key Concepts
Effective Health (EHP): High armor increases your total effective health against physical hits, meaning healers have more time to react before you are defeated.
Diminishing Returns vs. Linear Scaling: Each point of armor adds a linear amount of physical survivability, even though the character sheet percentage curve slows down as you stack more. 

Fandom
Modifiers: Armor works alongside other Damage mitigation mechanics like blocking with shields, passive class bonuses, and external buffs or debuffs (such as Demoralizing Shout reducing enemy attack power). 
