How to Implement This in Your Game Engine
When building your game, you shouldn't use a hardcoded value for K. Instead, scale K based on the Attacker's Level (or the player's level) so armor doesn't become overpowered as characters progress. 
Step 1: Define K based on Level
Create a function that calculates K dynamically. For example, if you want a level 1 player to hit 50% mitigation at 100 armor, but a level 50 player to need 5,000 armor:
