Step 2: Calculate Damage Mitigation
Apply the formula to calculate incoming damage. Ensure you also implement a hard cap so players can't break the game's combat tuning if they find an armor exploit. 

Fandom
csharp
int CalculateMitigatedDamage(int rawDamage, float armorPoints, int attackerLevel) {
    float K = CalculateKConstant(attackerLevel);
    
    // 1. Calculate raw reduction percentage
    float damageReduction = armorPoints / (armorPoints + K);
    
    // 2. Enforce a WoW-style maximum cap (e.g., 75% max reduction)
    if (damageReduction > 0.75f) {
        damageReduction = 0.75f;
    }
    
    // 3. Apply the reduction to the incoming damage
    float finalDamage = rawDamage * (1f - damageReduction);
    
    // Round to integer for final health subtraction
    return Mathf.RoundToInt(finalDamage);
}
