Why This Formula is Great for Game Designers
Perfect Effective Health (EHP) Scaling: Every single point of armor added increases a character's "Effective Health" against physical damage by a perfectly flat, linear amount. If a player has 1,000 HP, and K = 1000, every 1 point of armor gives them exactly 1 more point of "raw damage" durability. They will never feel like an armor upgrade was wasted. 

Fandom
Easy Balance Control: If you notice that tanks are surviving way too long in endgame content, you don't need to manually rebalance thousands of pieces of armor gear. You just subtly increase the value of K for high-level raid bosses, and everyone's armor naturally scales down in effectiveness against those specific enemies
